# 5.  Architecture Rules (Rules 1–10, Permanent)

| **Rule** | **Statement** |
| --- | --- |
| Rule 1 | Scope pill drives visibility of data, not ownership of tasks. |
| Rule 2 | One filter function per data type: getScopeShows(), lcScopeFilter(), canView(), canViewInScope(), getKpiScopeValue(). |
| Rule 3 | Identity scope (who you are) is independent of scope pill (what you are viewing). |
| Rule 4 | Never hardcode scope assumptions into workspace render functions. |
| Rule 5 | Declare filter contract before building any workspace. |
| Rule 6 | Visibility ≠ ownership. A leader can see records they do not own. |
| Rule 7 | resetWorkspaceState() is called on every showPage() to prevent stale selections. |
| Rule 8 | All modals use .lc-modal-overlay pattern. No legacy .modal-bg usage. |
| Rule 9 | Checklist advance buttons and approval bars use 8px border-radius (pending cleanup pass). |
| Rule 10 | onScopeChanged() must handle every built page explicitly — no silent failures on scope switch. |

# 6.  Identity & Scope Architecture

Two independent dimensions drive all data visibility:

- Identity Scope — who you are; drives LC record ownership, task checkability, and stat tile ownership

- Scope Pill — Enterprise / Region / Branch; drives shows, KPIs, and sidebar visibility

## Identity Directory (37 leaders)

- craig / nesana — enterprise, ES level, task role: es

- ellen, lubi, maud, lisette, leslie — Regional Directors

- jennifer.vaughan — Off-Site region

- Branch-level Hiring Managers: h1 through h18

- erii — admin

# 7.  Filter Functions

| **Function** | **Drives** |
| --- | --- |
| getScopeShows() | Shows in Staffing & Scheduling + Active Events |
| lcScopeFilter() | LC record visibility in sidebar lists |
| canView() | Recruiting ownership + stat tiles |
| canViewInScope() | Recruiting visibility in sidebar |
| getKpiScopeValue() | KPI metric values by scope |

# 8.  Role Title Standard (Locked)

"Exhibitor Services" is always spelled in full. Never abbreviated to "ES" as a title prefix. Eleven roles: Coordinator through Sr. Director.

# 9.  Recruiting & Hiring Workspace

13 tasks in sequential order, stage-gated. Key decisions:

- t2 (Compensation Review) is owned by the RD, not the HM — skipped for HMs whose direct manager is an RD

- t13 gate: offer letter must be sent before a position can be marked filled

- Stat tiles: Open Requisitions, In Process, Offer Stage, Filled (YTD)

- "In Process" label (no hyphen) — locked permanently

- Advance buttons use 8px border-radius — deferred cleanup pass

- h4 (Lubi Garza / San Antonio) is the canonical end-to-end test case — t2 is not skipped because the HM is not the RD

# 10.  Onboarding Workspace

32 tasks across 3 phases:

- Phase 1: Pre-arrival (HM tasks before new hire start date)

- Phase 2: First week

- Phase 3: First 90 days

Records are created automatically when a candidate accepts an offer in Recruiting & Hiring.

# 11.  Transitions Workspace

Two flows:

- Promotion — internal move up within the organization

- Transfer Out — lateral move or branch change

Both flows include a backfill handoff trigger — see Section 13 for full architecture.

# 12.  Offboarding Workspace

Two flows:

- Resignation

- Termination

Both flows include a backfill handoff trigger — see Section 13 for full architecture.

# 13.  Backfill Handoff Architecture

When a Transition or Offboarding record reaches the backfill trigger task, a pre-populated Recruiting record is created automatically with the following inherited values:

- Role — inherited from departing person

- Branch — inherited from departing person

- Hiring Manager — inherited from scope

- Backfill flag — set to true

- Source record ID — linked to originating TR or OFF record

The inline override button in the Recruiting modal allows the HM to adjust role and FT/PT status before confirming the backfill record.

# 14.  Staffing & Scheduling Workspace

## SHOWS Data Object

705 NSS shows loaded from ES_National_Show_Schedule.xlsx. Each show record contains:

**Original fields (present since initial build):**

name, city, facility, region, showOpen, showClose, moveInStart, clearDate, currentBooths, projectedBooths, pyBooths, revenueActuals, sfRevenue, pyJobNumber, freemanPlatform, freemanAV, freemanElectrical, freemanElectricalOnly, fte, perLbMH, producingBranch

**Added in v6.31 (Events Lens enrichment — all 705 shows):**

discountDate, advFreightDate, showClosePlus8, rdName, directors[ ], supervisor, lead, offsitePrep, offsitePost, growthOwner, growthAE, serviceDesk, serviceModel, standardModel, customReason, onSiteReps, remoteReps, totalReps, boothRange, orderPct, pyOrderPct

## Staffing Model (MODEL Array)

15 booth tiers from 1–750 booths, each defining cf (customer-facing), br (back room), as (additional support), sv (supervisory) counts. Freight/storage desk (fr) always defaults to 0 — user-entered only.

## ssCalcRec() Function

Derives staffing model recommendation from booth count and revenue. Revenue overlay: if revenue > $2M AND revenue > tier average, adds extra back room roles. Supervisor triggered independently if revenue > $2M regardless of booth tier.

## Five Staffing UI Flows

| **Flow** | **Trigger** | **Description** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 — Remote eligibility | Booth count below threshold | Prompts whether to use remote service model |
| 2 — Standard model | Normal booth count | Recommends model from MODEL array based on booth count |
| 3 — Custom plan | 751+ booths | Allows manual entry of all 5 staffing categories |
| 4 — Confirmed plan | Plan has been confirmed | Locked view with Edit button to modify |
| 5 — Completion popup | All tasks complete | Show-close confirmation and summary |

## Cross-Link to Events Lens

- Job number in Staffing sidebar is clickable → goToEventLens() — stopPropagation prevents sidebar show selection from also firing

- Staffing detail panel has "View full event profile ↗" tlink next to every job number

- goToSsFromEvents() links back from Events Lens staffing card to the full staffing plan

# 15.  Lens Pages Architecture

Lens pages are entity-centric — they cut across all process workspaces and aggregate everything known about a single entity. They are distinct from process-centric workspaces.

| **Lens** | **Entity Unit** | **Status** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| KPIs | Metric / aggregate | ✅ Built |
| Events | Single show (job number) | ✅ Built |
| Team | Person or whole team | ⏳ Placeholder — design not started |
| Customers | Customer / account | ⏳ Placeholder — Qualtrics integration required |

*Key architectural decision: The Events Lens is the canonical home base for any show referenced anywhere in the site. All show references site-wide link to it. The pattern is: action → event (not action → staffing page).*

# 16.  Events Lens — Full Specification

## Entry Points

| **Entry Point** | **Trigger** | **Function Called** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| goToEventLens(showId) | Universal — called from anywhere in the site | Direct navigation to Events Lens |
| Active Events cards (Today's Priorities) | Click any active event card | goToShow() → goToEventLens() |
| Staffing & Scheduling detail panel | "View full event profile ↗" tlink | goToEventLens(ssSelId) |
| Staffing & Scheduling sidebar | Click job number | goToEventLens(sid) + stopPropagation |
| Search bar on Events page | Type show name or job number | elSelectShow() → elRenderShow() |
| Direct URL / back navigation | elSelId persists last-viewed show | initEvents() → elRenderShow() |

## Page Structure

Page header: "Events" (page-title 21.6px/800) + "Look up any show by job number" (page-sub 14px/muted) — matching .page-hdr pattern used on all other pages.

Search bar: 1.5px border, 9px border-radius, 14px input, live dropdown up to 10 results showing name, city, branch, open date. Dropdown closes on outside click.

Show header: Show name (21.6px/800), meta row (facility, city, branch, RD name), chip flags row (platform, service model, custom staffing, FTE, AV, electrical, MH, exhibitor store link, prior year job #).

## Event Timeline Card

7 milestones on a horizontal progress track:

| **Milestone** | **Data Field** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Discount deadline | discountDate | NSS: Discount Price Deadline Date |
| Advance freight deadline | advFreightDate | NSS: Advance Freight Receiving Deadline Date |
| Exhibitor move-in start | moveInStart | NSS: Move-In Start Date |
| Show open | showOpen | NSS: Show Open Date |
| Show close | showClose | NSS: Show Close Date |
| Exhibitor clear | clearDate | NSS: Clear Date |
| Show close +8 | showClosePlus8 | NSS col HX: 8th Business Day Date — distinctive navy dot |

Progress track fills green for completed milestones based on today's date. Dot states: green checkmark = done, gold fill = active/today, white outline with gray border = upcoming, navy fill = show close +8.

*Label convention (locked): "Event Timeline" — not "Show Timeline"*

## Event Scale & Revenue (3 Stat Tiles)

| **Tile** | **Primary Value** | **Supporting Detail** | **Accent Color** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Current booths | currentBooths (formatted with comma) | vs projectedBooths; YoY delta vs pyBooths | --mb blue |
| Revenue actuals | revenueActuals (formatted $X.XXM) | vs sfRevenue projection; order rate % | Green |
| Current order % | orderPct (X.X%) | prior year pyOrderPct; delta in pts ▲/▼ | Gold |

*Design decision: Current order % is the headline value. Prior year is supporting context — not the reverse. Delta shown as ▲/▼ pts.*

*Label convention (locked): "Event Scale **&** Revenue" — not "Show Scale **&** Revenue"*

## Three-Column Row: Staffing Plan / ES Team / Growth Contacts

Staffing Plan card:

- 5 role categories derived from ssCalcRec(): Customer-facing, Back room, Additional support, Supervisory, Freight/storage desk

- Total rep count displayed in navy highlight bar at bottom

- Standard model flag — green "Yes" or orange "No — [custom reason]"

- Off-site hours removed from this card

- "Off-Site — Post" field suppressed when NSS value is "Branch" (placeholder, not a person)

- "📋 View confirmed staffing plan ↗" or "📋 Open in Staffing & Scheduling ↗" link depending on plan confirmation state

ES Team card:

- Rows: Regional Director, Directors/Managers (collapsed with +N), On-Site Supervisor, On-Site Lead, Off-Site Prep (if not "Branch")

- Service desk phone number at bottom of this card — separated by divider with phone icon

- Service desk was deliberately moved here from the Staffing Plan card

Growth Contacts card:

- Opportunity Owner only

- Producing AE only

- "Off-site support" and all lines below it removed

## Placeholder Rows

Team Operations (2-col): ESM task compliance (SERF, NERF, FOL, show close) | Timekeeping & hours (Workfront)

Service Excellence (3-col): Post-show survey results (Qualtrics) | Service requests (Salesforce) | BBB / social media

## State Persistence

elSelId persists the last-viewed show. Navigating away and back restores the show. Same pattern as ssSelId in Staffing & Scheduling.

# 17.  Cross-Site Integration Map

| **Source Location** | **Trigger** | **Destination** | **Function** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Today's Priorities — Active Events cards | Click card | Events Lens | goToShow() → goToEventLens() |
| Staffing & Scheduling — Detail panel | "View full event profile ↗" tlink | Events Lens | goToEventLens(ssSelId) |
| Staffing & Scheduling — Sidebar job# | Click job number (stopPropagation) | Events Lens | goToEventLens(sid) |
| Events Lens — Staffing plan card | "Open in Staffing & Scheduling ↗" | Staffing & Scheduling | goToSsFromEvents(elSelId) |
| Needs Attention cards (future) | When show-linked tasks added | Events Lens | goToEventLens() — infrastructure ready |

*Key decision: goToShow() was the original Active Events routing function targeting Staffing **&** Scheduling. It has been permanently rerouted to call goToEventLens() instead. Events Lens is the show home base — this is not reversible.*

