The Events Lens mockup went through a formal design audit against the live build before implementation. Eight corrections were applied:

| **Property** | **Live Build Standard** | **Correction Applied** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Font sizes | 14px body, 13.5px meta, 21.6px titles | Scaled up from 11–12px in original mockup |
| Font weight on stat values | 900 | Bumped from 800 |
| Card borders | 1px solid #E2E5EF | Changed from 0.5px |
| Card border-radius | 10px | Changed from 12px |
| Chip font size | 14px / font-weight 700 | Changed from 11px |
| Page header | .page-hdr with title + sub | Added — was missing from original mockup |
| Job number style | --mb blue text, inline | Changed from white-on-navy pill chip |
| Placeholder style | White bg, solid border, emoji icon | Changed from dashed border on surface background |

# 19.  KPI Workspace

9 KPIs, fully scope-aware. KPI sidebar + detail panel. Scope breakdowns shown per KPI in a 3-column grid. All values respond dynamically to Enterprise / Region / Branch scope pill.

# 20.  Platform Chip Design Decisions

Freeman Now and Freeman Next chips appear in two locations with deliberately different styling:

| **Location** | **Freeman Next** | **Freeman Now** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Active Events (Today's Priorities) | Light blue tint #CBF0FC, dark teal text #005A75, 2px border #7DD9F3 | Light gold tint #FFF4D6, dark amber text #7A5200, 2px border #FFD166 |
| Staffing & Scheduling detail panel | Light blue pill (ss-pill-blue class) | Light blue pill (same style as Next) |

*Rationale: In Staffing detail, platform is one data point among several equals — uniform styling appropriate. In Active Events, blue vs. gold creates immediate at-a-glance distinction since platform is the primary differentiator between cards.*

# 21.  Needs Attention Panel

Confirmed fully dynamic — no hardcoded cards remain. The panel draws from four live data sources, filtered through needsMyAction() and lcNeedsAction():

- Recruiting — hires filtered by needsMyAction()

- Onboarding — obRecords via lcNeedsAction()

- Transitions — trRecords via lcNeedsAction()

- Offboarding — offRecords via lcNeedsAction()

*Code comment confirms: "Hardcoded placeholder items removed — pending process timeline definition"*

Future integration: when show-linked tasks are added to Needs Attention, those cards will carry goToEventLens() links. The infrastructure is in place.

